Model Comparison Insight:
=>Logistic Regression performs well for linear separable text data and is faster.
=>SVM can handle high-dimensional TF-IDF features effectively.
=>Based on results:
    -If SVM > LR → better margin separation
    -If LR ≈ SVM → simpler model preferred
    
Cross-validation insight:
=>CV scores confirm model stability.
=>Small variance → model is reliable
=>Large variance → model overfitting

Word2Vec Embedding Technique:
Word2Vec is an advanced NLP embedding technique used to convert words into dense numerical vectors. Unlike TF-IDF, Word2Vec captures semantic relationships between words and provides contextual meaning.
In this implementation:
=>The cleaned reviews were tokenized into individual words.
=>A Word2Vec model was trained using the tokenized reviews.
=>Each word was converted into a 100-dimensional vector representation.
=>Average word vectors were calculated for every review to create feature vectors.
=>These feature vectors were used to train a Logistic Regression model for sentiment classification.
=>This approach helps improve text representation by capturing similarities and relationships between words more effectively than traditional frequency-based methods.